<title>GERMANY: Daimler says to cut sick pay to 80 pct. [CORRECTED 13:55 GMT]</title>
<headline>Daimler says to cut sick pay to 80 pct. [CORRECTED 13:55 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects headline and text to show sick pay will be cut to 80 percent, not by 80 percent.)</p>
<p>Daimler-Benz AG, taking a cue from government calls for industry to help reduce Germany's welfare state, said on Tuesday it was cutting sick pay for its employees to 80 percent from October 1.</p>
<p>Earlier this month, the Bonn government called on employers to adjust sick pay agreements in expiring contracts as part of a package of measures to cut government spending and make Germany more competitive.</p>
</text>
